═══════════════════════════════════════════
IF THE DROPLET WAS DESTROYED — REBUILD FROM SCRATCH
═══════════════════════════════════════════

Full sequence, in order, with the gotchas we've hit before baked in:

1. Create a new droplet: 4 vCPU / 8GB RAM minimum (2vCPU/4GB caused
   memory-pressure/swap-thrashing problems before), Ubuntu, same region
   (NYC1) if it matters for latency.

2. Create + activate a 4GB swap file BEFORE bringing up the stack:

    fallocate -l 4G /swapfile
    chmod 600 /swapfile
    mkswap /swapfile
    swapon /swapfile
    echo '/swapfile none swap sw 0 0' >> /etc/fstab
    free -h    # confirm Swap: 4.0Gi

3. Install Docker:

    curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sh

4. Generate a new SSH deploy key on the droplet and add it to the GitHub
   repo (the old one dies with the old droplet — this is NOT reused):

    ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "acdt-droplet" -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 -N ""
    cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub   # add this to GitHub repo deploy keys

5. Clone the repo:

    git clone git@github.com:jstsirabor/acdt-camry.git
    cd acdt-camry

6. Recreate .env from scratch — EVERY value needs retyping (this file is
   gitignored on purpose and does NOT survive a destroy). Keep your saved
   copy handy. Required sections: Ollama, Influx, Mongo, Neo4j, Ditto +
   Mechanic Ditto, OpenWeather/OpenRoute keys, MQTT block, and the model
   vars (see MODELS section below).

7. python3 -m venv .venv will likely fail with "ensurepip is not
   available" — fix first:

    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install -y python3.12-venv python3-pip
    python3 -m venv .venv
    source .venv/bin/activate

8. pip install -r requirements.txt will likely fail on
   torch==2.12.0+cpu (not on regular PyPI) — install it separately first:

    pip install torch==2.12.0+cpu --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
    pip install -r requirements.txt

   Confirm paho-mqtt installed cleanly (needed for the MQTT data source):

    pip show paho-mqtt

9. Bring up the Docker stack:

    docker compose up -d
    docker ps

   Check InfluxDB SPECIFICALLY shows a real port mapping
   (0.0.0.0:8086->8086/tcp, not just 8086/tcp with no host binding) —
   this has silently failed before after a port conflict.

10. Recreate the acdt.service systemd unit:

    sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/acdt.service

[Unit]
Description=ACDT Camry App
After=docker.service network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target
Requires=docker.service

[Service]
Type=simple
WorkingDirectory=/root/acdt-camry
ExecStart=/root/acdt-camry/.venv/bin/python /root/acdt-camry/main.py
Restart=always
RestartSec=5
User=root
EnvironmentFile=/root/acdt-camry/.env

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target

    sudo systemctl daemon-reload
    sudo systemctl enable acdt.service
    sudo systemctl start acdt.service
    sudo systemctl status acdt.service

11. Verify end-to-end (see TESTING section below for the full checklist) —
    data source, sensors, ATDT diagnose/guidance, dashboards.

Note on logs: this rebuilt service does NOT use a StandardOutput=append
log file — logs go through journalctl, NOT a plain acdt.log file (despite
what an older version of this doc said):

    journalctl -u acdt.service -n 50 --no-pager
    journalctl -u acdt.service --since "5 minutes ago" --no-pager
    journalctl -u acdt.service -f     # follow live

═══════════════════════════════════════════
PRODUCTION (droplet) — day to day
═══════════════════════════════════════════

1. SSH in

    ssh root@<CURRENT_DROPLET_IP>    # check DO panel if unsure
    cd ~/acdt-camry
    source .venv/bin/activate

2. Bring up the Docker stack (both Ditto clusters + all infra)

    docker compose up -d
    docker ps

Every container should show a PORTS mapping. You're running TWO Ditto
stacks side by side:
  - Main Ditto  → gateway on :8081, nginx on :8080  (vehicle digital twin)
  - Mechanic Ditto → gateway on :8091, nginx on :8090 (mechanic's twin,
    Thing ID org.example:MECHANIC_001)

If anything shows a blank PORTS column, force it to recreate:

    docker compose stop <container_name>
    docker compose rm -f <container_name>
    docker compose up -d <container_name>

3. Backend runs as a systemd service — no manual `python main.py` needed

    systemctl status acdt.service      # check it's running
    systemctl restart acdt.service     # after a git pull / .env change
    systemctl stop acdt.service        # to fully stop it

Logs via journalctl (see rebuild section above):

    journalctl -u acdt.service -n 50 --no-pager
    journalctl -u acdt.service --since "5 minutes ago" --no-pager | grep -i error

4. Deploying a code change

    # locally: edit, commit, push
    git add . && git commit -m "..." && git push

    # on droplet:
    git pull
    systemctl restart acdt.service
    sleep 5    # give Ditto/Neo4j provisioning time before hitting the API
    journalctl -u acdt.service -n 30 --no-pager     # confirm clean startup

Gotcha: if git pull fails with "untracked working tree files would be
overwritten," something local isn't committed (e.g. a test script you
forgot to add). Move it aside, pull, then decide whether to keep it:

    mv <file> <file>.bak && git pull

Tip: before restarting, sanity-check a Python file isn't broken —

    python3 -c "import ast; ast.parse(open('path/to/file.py').read())" && echo "Syntax OK"

Gotcha: HTML/static files served by the app must match the EXACT filename
the backend expects (e.g. ui/mechanic.html) — saving/pushing under a
different name (e.g. mechanic_console.html) causes a FileNotFoundError /
500 on that route. Confirm the route works after any UI file change:

    curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" localhost:8501/mechanic

5. .env — required on BOTH the droplet and your local machine separately
   (.env is gitignored, changes don't sync, and does NOT survive a
   droplet destroy — keep an external saved copy)

    DITTO_URL / DITTO_USER / DITTO_PASSWORD          → main Ditto (:8080)
    MECHANIC_DITTO_URL=http://localhost:8090
    MECHANIC_DITTO_USER=ditto
    MECHANIC_DITTO_PASSWORD=ditto
    MECHANIC_THING_ID=org.example:MECHANIC_001
    OBD_MODE=mqtt   # or adapter/simulator/auto — can also be overridden
                     # live via the mechanic console's data-source toggle,
                     # which takes priority over this and needs no restart

═══════════════════════════════════════════
MODELS — which LLM drives what
═══════════════════════════════════════════

All models run locally via Ollama (OLLAMA_HOST/OLLAMA_API_KEY in .env) —
no cloud LLM API, no VLM (system is text/sensor-data driven, not
image-based).

    SAFETY_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b            # smaller/faster, real-time checks
    PREVENTIVE_MODEL=gpt-oss:120b
    PREDICTIVE_MODEL=gpt-oss:120b
    DIAGNOSTIC_MODEL=gpt-oss:120b       # ATDT diagnose — not in .env,
    GUIDANCE_MODEL=gpt-oss:120b         # falls back to shared/config.py
                                        # default if unset

