LOCAL DEV (before pushing to droplet)
═══════════════════════════════════════════

Only needed if you're testing code changes before deploying. Requires a
local .env with the same MECHANIC_* values pointed at a local Ditto stack,
or the mechanic push will just fail/fallback to local Mongo storage
(harmless, but won't test the real integration).

    cd ~/Documents/Tech/acdt-camry
    sudo docker compose up -d
    sudo docker compose ps
    source .venv/bin/activate
    python main.py

Watch for:
    [MAIN] Waiting for Ditto gateway...
    [DITTO] Policy: 204
    [DITTO] Thing: 204
    [MAIN] Waiting for Neo4j...
    [NEO4J] Knowledge graph ready.
    [MAIN] Starting Ditto sync...
    [OBD READER] Mode: MQTT (cloud broker)
    [MQTT READER] Connected to 77426ba5e0b34670b30bf6f00a354af9.s1.eu.hivemq.cloud
    [OBD READER] ✅ MQTT subscriber started, waiting for ESP32 data...
    [MAIN] Live data writer started (real telemetry → InfluxDB while
           adapter/mqtt is the active source)
    [MAIN] Dashboard → http://localhost:8501

(Optional) Real vehicle data instead of simulator: plug in the ELM327,
ignition on, power on the ESP32, watch its Serial Monitor for
"[MQTT] Published OBD data". Without this, either the simulator or
mqtt_fake_publisher.py (see TESTING section above) works fine for
end-to-end testing without the car present.

Local dashboards: http://localhost:8501 and http://localhost:8501/mechanic
From another device on the same network: swap localhost for the host
machine's LAN IP (`hostname -I`).

Shut down locally: Ctrl+C the main.py terminal, then
`sudo docker compose down`.
